# The rules of the build and dependencies self-audit: what must hold for Traceworks' build (docs/architecture.md:
# few dependencies, only Jackson at runtime; a reproducible build; pinned images), and where the tool looks.
# A broken rule turns the gate RED. The format is described in the package's README.md.

# Outside the test scope only Jackson and Traceworks' own modules (the modules of the reactor are always allowed).
runtime-allow    com.fasterxml.jackson.core:*
runtime-allow    io.github.flsest:*

# maven-enforcer-plugin guards the line above in every build: its bannedDependencies must allow exactly that.
require          enforcer-guard

# Two builds of one commit give the same jar.
require          output-timestamp
java-release     21

# The plugins that shape traceworks.jar or run its tests come from the POMs, not from the Maven that runs the build.
plugin-pinned    maven-compiler-plugin maven-resources-plugin maven-jar-plugin maven-surefire-plugin

# Pre-releases (alpha, beta, M1, rc, ...) and qualified builds (byte-buddy's -jdk5) are no update.
stable-version   ^\d+(\.\d+)*$

maven-repository https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2
npm-registry     https://registry.npmjs.org

# Every base image of the Dockerfiles below is on Docker Hub; the registries step asks no other image registry.
image-registry   docker.io

# The images Traceworks ships and the images of its packages. The fake images of the integration tests are not
# shipped and stay out.
dockerfile       images/*/Dockerfile
dockerfile       examples/**/images/*/Dockerfile

accept           package_unpinned images/shell/Dockerfile The shell image installs Debian's current packages on purpose, and the record names the image ID each container started from (docs/security.md, "Images and containers").

# The Maven image of the two mutation-testing packages, byte-identical copies, so one line for each.
accept           package_unpinned examples/mutation-testing/images/maven/Dockerfile The Maven image installs Ubuntu's current git and openssh-client on purpose: Ubuntu removes a superseded version from its archive, so a pinned version would break the build at its next security update. The record names the image ID each container started from (docs/security.md, "Images and containers").
accept           package_unpinned examples/mutation-testing-grounded/images/maven/Dockerfile The Maven image installs Ubuntu's current git and openssh-client on purpose: Ubuntu removes a superseded version from its archive, so a pinned version would break the build at its next security update. The record names the image ID each container started from (docs/security.md, "Images and containers").
